# SPA DRAG — dogfight mass, homepage, nav
File: website/audit/spa-drag.oot

Verdict: PASS on the two-homepage lie after the 2026-09-04
repair. The dogfight remains by product choice. It is split
to files at most 256 lines.

## 1. Homepage

`index.html` `#content` holds one install box and the
`pulled/openOODA.oot` body as real HTML. No-JS and crawlers
see that body. JS fetch replaces it from the `.oot` file.
If the fetch fails and `.install` is already in the DOM, the
static body stays. Copy buttons bind on the static body.

There is no second card set. There is no `cli` route.

## 2. Dogfight mass

The product path is route + markdown + theme + install.
The dogfight is the rest of `src/dogfight/`. It stays. Do
not delete it unless the owner asks.

`404.html` still loads the dogfight scripts so the 404 page
matches home visually. That is extra bytes on a miss.

## 3. WASM residue

No WASM module loads from this repo. `window.wasmActive` is
not read. Dead WASM route wrappers are gone.

## 4. Nav order (substratum first)

Law of Substratum Integrity (RULES.oot §1.20) and RFC-0004
3-layer order:

1. openOODA — strategic law
2. oodar — Gen 1 host
3. oodac — Gen 2 compiler
4. std — library
5. ooda — operational driver
6. packaging — how bits land on a machine
7. opm — package manager
8. catalog — what opm search reads
9. lsp — editor protocol
10. mcp — agent protocol

website and .github are table-only. They are not product
nav routes.

## 5. Next repair

Optional: drop dogfight scripts from `404.html`. Optional:
pre-render the other nine routes as static HTML. Do not do
either unless asked.
